Looking at your pod definition, I can see the exact problem now.

The Problem
The Nginx container mounts the shared volume at /var/www/html, but the Nginx config (from the nginx-config ConfigMap) is almost certainly pointing its root directive to /usr/share/nginx/html — the default Nginx document root. Meanwhile, the PHP-FPM container mounts the shared volume at /usr/share/nginx/html.

So the shared emptyDir volume is mounted at:

php-fpm-container → /usr/share/nginx/html

nginx-container → /var/www/html

These are two different paths on the same shared volume... which actually still works for sharing files, but the discrepancy is what's tripping you up. The standard fix for this lab is to make both containers mount at /var/www/html so they agree with the Nginx config's root directive, and then copy index.php there.

You also have a YAML syntax error in your pasted file (terminationMessagePath is dedented under nginx-container) — likely just a copy-paste artifact, but worth fixing if it's in the real file.

What to Change
Change 1 — php-fpm-container volumeMount
yaml
# BEFORE
    volumeMounts:
    - mountPath: /usr/share/nginx/html
      name: shared-files

# AFTER
    volumeMounts:
    - mountPath: /var/www/html
      name: shared-files
Change 2 — nginx-container volumeMount
Leave it as /var/www/html (it's already correct):

yaml
    volumeMounts:
    - mountPath: /var/www/html
      name: shared-files
