    terminationMessagePolicy: File
    volumeMounts:
    ...
Apply the Fix
bash
kubectl delete pod nginx-phpfpm
kubectl apply -f nginx-phpfpm.yaml
Wait for it to be Running:

bash
kubectl get pod nginx-phpfpm -w
Copy the File
bash
kubectl cp /home/thor/index.php nginx-phpfpm:/var/www/html/index.php -c nginx-container
⚠️ Heads-up on kubectl cp: kubectl cp writes into the container's filesystem via the container runtime, not through the shared volume. Since nginx-container has the emptyDir mounted at /var/www/html, copying to /var/www/html/index.php inside nginx-container does land on the shared volume — so php-fpm-container will see it too at /var/www/html/index.php. That's exactly what you want.

Verify
bash
kubectl exec nginx-phpfpm -c nginx-container -- ls -l /var/www/html/
kubectl exec nginx-phpfpm -c php-fpm-container -- ls -l /var/www/html/
Both should show index.php. Then hit the Website button on the top bar — the PHP page should render.

