You're almost there — the file is in place and the config looks correct. But there's one remaining bug in the Nginx config that will prevent PHP from working.

The Remaining Issue: fastcgi_pass 127.0.0.1:9000
Look at this line in the ConfigMap:

text
fastcgi_pass 127.0.0.1:9000;
This tells Nginx to connect to PHP-FPM on 127.0.0.1 (localhost). But Nginx and PHP-FPM are in two separate containers within the same pod — they share a network namespace (so localhost is shared between them via the pod IP)...

Actually wait — let me be precise here. In Kubernetes, containers in the same pod do share the network namespace, so 127.0.0.1:9000 from the nginx-container will reach the php-fpm-container on port 9000. So this should work...

However, there's a second problem: PHP-FPM by default listens on a Unix socket (/var/run/php-fpm.sock or similar), not on TCP port 9000. The php:7.2-fpm-alpine image's default www.conf listens on 127.0.0.1:9000 — so that part is actually fine out of the box.

Let me re-check what's actually broken.

Let's Actually Test It
Try hitting the website and see what happens:

bash
kubectl exec nginx-phpfpm -c nginx-container -- curl -s http://localhost:8099/
Or from the jump host (if you can reach the pod):

bash
kubectl get pod nginx-phpfpm -o wide   # get pod IP
curl http://<pod-ip>:8099/
You should also verify Nginx config is valid and PHP-FPM is actually listening:

bash
# Check nginx config is loaded correctly
kubectl exec nginx-phpfpm -c nginx-container -- nginx -t

# Check what PHP-FPM is listening on
kubectl exec nginx-phpfpm -c php-fpm-container -- netstat -tlnp 2>/dev/null || \
kubectl exec nginx-phpfpm -c php-fpm-container -- ss -tlnp

# Check nginx error log
kubectl exec nginx-phpfpm -c nginx-container -- cat /var/log/nginx/error.log
What to Look For
If curl returns the PHP output correctly → you're done, the task is complete. Just click the Website button.

If you get a 502 Bad Gateway → PHP-FPM isn't reachable on 127.0.0.1:9000. That would mean PHP-FPM is listening on a Unix socket instead. Fix by either:

Changing the ConfigMap's fastcgi_pass to unix:/var/run/php-fpm.sock; (matching PHP-FPM's socket), or

Configuring PHP-FPM's www.conf to listen on 127.0.0.1:9000.

If you get a 404 → the try_files in location / is fine, but your index.php should still be found. Check the file is really there (it is, per your ls).

If you get the raw PHP source → Nginx isn't matching the .php location block. That would be odd given the config.

My Suspicion
Given your ls output shows index.php present in both containers at /var/www/html, and the ConfigMap correctly sets root /var/www/html and fastcgi_pass 127.0.0.1:9000, the setup should already work. Run the curl test above to confirm:

bash
kubectl exec nginx-phpfpm -c nginx-container -- curl -s http://127.0.0.1:8099/
If that returns your PHP page's output (e.g., <?php echo "Hello"; ?> rendered as Hello), then you're finished — just click the Website button on the top bar and confirm. The ls output already proves both containers share the file correctly, and the ConfigMap grep shows the config is right.

One small note: your terminal shows a typo in the kubectl cp line (-c nginx-containerer with a stray er), but since the subsequent ls shows index.php present in both containers, the copy clearly succeeded (the shell may have autocorrected or you re-ran it). So no action needed there.

Run the curl check and let me know what it returns — that'll tell us definitively whether anything else needs fixing.

